  "note": "Annual election of six urban councillors, January 1925; a seventh candidate withdrew, leaving six for the six vacancies, who were declared elected unopposed (Belfast News-Letter, 7 January 1925, p. 11). One withdrawal was made from the seven candidates nominated: Mr. William Henry Elliott, who was the only candidate nominated for re-election. The paper says the other six, all new members, 'will be duly declared elected to the six vacancies'. The nomination report (BNL 6 Jan 1925 p. 6) names the sixth candidate David C. Campbell; the 7 Jan report and the 1928 list of retiring members name him David C. Thompson/Thomson (gap-fill 6 Nov 2026). Returned unopposed."
